            "count": 0,
            "text": "Created attachment 3767\nCandidate patch.\n\nTo reproduce:\n\n```\nm <- matrix(1:4, 2)\n\nmm <- m; mm[[-1, 1]] <- 99L\nmm[, 1]\n\n## `[[` reads an uninitialized int in the same argument position:\nres <- replicate(200, {\n  invisible(lapply(1:200, function(i) c(2L, 2L)))   # churn the heap\n  tryCatch(as.character(m[[-1, 1]]), error = function(e) \"<error>\")\n})\ntable(res)\n```\n\nThis gives me:\n\n```\n> mm <- m; mm[[-1, 1]] <- 99L\n> mm[, 1]\n[1]  1 99\n>\n> ## `[[` reads an uninitialized int in the same argument position:\n> res <- replicate(200, {\n+   invisible(lapply(1:200, function(i) c(2L, 2L)))   # churn the heap\n+   tryCatch(as.character(m[[-1, 1]]), error = function(e) \"<error>\")\n+ })\n> table(res)\nres\n<error>       2\n    173      27\n```\n\nbut note that the number of errors here isn't deterministic.\n\nFrom what I can see, the issue here arises because of the use of `pindx` instead of `pdims` in the invocation of `get1index()`. Note that the same loop form is used in `do_subassign2_dflt()` (`subassign.c:1897-1911`), but with `pdims[i]` passed instead, so I suspect this is a long-standing typo.",
            "bug_id": 19116
          }
        ]
      }
